From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:45:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: stop queueing capture reads after STOP

Since commit cee3e63e7106 ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: do not set stream
state in event and trigger callbacks") the trigger STOP only sends EOS
and the stream state stays RUNNING until the next prepare or close. The
READ_DONE handler requeues a read whenever that state is RUNNING, so after
STOP every READ_DONE from the DSP queues the next read, and the driver
keeps calling snd_pcm_period_elapsed() for a stream that ALSA has
stopped, until the application prepares or closes the PCM.

Requeue a read only while ALSA runs the stream (RUNNING) or will resume
it without a prepare (PAUSED, or SUSPENDED from one of these). Check the
ALSA state under the PCM stream lock, after the period accounting and
together with sending the read, so a concurrent or XRUN stop is seen.
ALSA sets that state itself, so this also covers a stop whose trigger
DPCM defers and a prepare from SUSPENDED, which skips the STOP trigger.
q6asm_read() only allocates with GFP_ATOMIC and sends without waiting,
like the trigger commands already sent under that lock.

The reads in flight at STOP complete without being requeued. The next
prepare closes the stream and queues a fresh set. A START rolled back
by STOP can still leave fewer reads queued for a retry without prepare.

Fixes: cee3e63e7106 ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: do not set stream state in event and trigger callbacks")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/71bac9c12f1e42521aeb825a7e2c3474b6114fb1
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
index c21f3201b82f67844b3ea2fbb8a557d0901dc10e..0adbcb2bed345c54cfbe51cbf0b10854a1eb71c8 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -179,11 +179,32 @@ static const struct snd_compr_codec_caps q6asm_compr_caps = {
 	.descriptor[0].formats = 0,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Requeue a capture read only while ALSA runs the stream. PAUSE and SUSPEND
+ * resume without a prepare that would queue the reads again, so they keep
+ * the reads in circulation. Called under the PCM stream lock.
+ */
+static bool q6asm_dai_requeue_read(struct snd_pcm_runtime *runtime)
+{
+	snd_pcm_state_t state;
+
+	if (!runtime)
+		return false;
+
+	state = runtime->state;
+	if (state == SNDRV_PCM_STATE_SUSPENDED)
+		state = runtime->suspended_state;
+
+	return state == SNDRV_PCM_STATE_RUNNING ||
+	       state == SNDRV_PCM_STATE_PAUSED;
+}
+
 static void event_handler(uint32_t opcode, uint32_t token,
 			  void *payload, void *priv)
 {
 	struct q6asm_dai_rtd *prtd = priv;
 	struct snd_pcm_substream *substream = prtd->substream;
+	unsigned long flags;
 
 	switch (opcode) {
 	case ASM_CLIENT_EVENT_CMD_RUN_DONE:
@@ -194,10 +215,12 @@ static void event_handler(uint32_t opcode, uint32_t token,
 		snd_pcm_period_elapsed(substream);
 		break;
 	case ASM_CLIENT_EVENT_DATA_READ_DONE:
-		snd_pcm_period_elapsed(substream);
-		if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING)
+		snd_pcm_stream_lock_irqsave(substream, flags);
+		snd_pcm_period_elapsed_under_stream_lock(substream);
+		if (prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING &&
+		    q6asm_dai_requeue_read(substream->runtime))
 			q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
-
+		snd_pcm_stream_unlock_irqrestore(substream, flags);
 		break;
 	default:
 		break;
